{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' test/dao/jing/mem_test.cljc | nl -ba -v1\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.jing.mem-test\n     2\t  \"Contract tests for dao.jing.mem/create-content-mem: the ephemeral\n     3\t   content-addressed in-memory DaoJing content store\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.jing.md, Materialization rule and Reads).\n     5\t\n     6\t   The handle is plain data carrying explicit private state plus\n     7\t   :put-content-fn, :get-content-fn, and :close-fn, and is consumed by\n     8\t   dao.jing/materialize!, dao.jing/get, and dao.jing/close!. It embeds no\n     9\t   intake stream and no source identity: addresses are derived solely from\n    10\t   payloads, equal payloads from a pool of intake streams converge on\n    11\t   exactly one entry, and an unequal payload at an existing address is an\n    12\t   integrity failure, never an overwrite.\"\n    13\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    14\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    15\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    16\t            [dao.stream :as ds]\n    17\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer]))\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t(defn throws?\n    21\t  \"True when (f) throws on every supported host.\"\n    22\t  [f]\n    23\t  (try (f)\n    24\t       false\n    25\t       (catch #?(:clj Exception\n    26\t                 :cljs :default\n    27\t                 :cljd Object)\n    28\t              _\n    29\t         true)))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(defn open-stream\n    33\t  \"Open a ringbuffer transport pre-loaded with vals.\"\n    34\t  [& vals]\n    35\t  (let [s (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer, :capacity 8})]\n    36\t    (doseq [v vals] (ds/append! s v))\n    37\t    s))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    41\t;; Handle shape\n    42\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    43\t\n    44\t(deftest create-content-mem-returns-a-stream-free-content-handle\n    45\t  (testing\n    46\t    \"the handle is plain data with explicit private state and the\n    47\t            three backend effects\"\n    48\t    (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)]\n    49\t      (is (map? h))\n    50\t      (is (fn? (:put-content-fn h)))\n    51\t      (is (fn? (:get-content-fn h)))\n    52\t      (is (fn? (:close-fn h)))\n    53\t      (is (= {:closed? false, :content {}} @(:state h)))))\n    54\t  (testing \"the handle embeds no intake stream and stores no source identity\"\n    55\t    (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)]\n    56\t      (is (not (contains? h :stream))\n    57\t          \"a content store carries no intake stream\")\n    58\t      (is (empty? (:content @(:state h)))))))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    62\t;; Opaque-payload contract\n    63\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    64\t\n    65\t(deftest materialize-mints-the-address-automatically\n    66\t  (testing\n    67\t    \"jing/materialize! derives the address from the payload alone and\n    68\t            the value round-trips unchanged\"\n    69\t    (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)\n    70\t          payload {:a 1, :b [1 2 3]}\n    71\t          address (jing/materialize! h payload)]\n    72\t      (is (= (jing/segment-key payload) address))\n    73\t      (is (= \"segment\" (namespace address)))\n    74\t      (is (= payload (jing/get h address ::missing)))\n    75\t      (is\n    76\t        (= {address payload} (:content @(:state h)))\n    77\t        \"exactly the payload is stored: no provenance stamp, no source identity\"))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(deftest opaque-payloads-round-trip-including-nil\n    81\t  (testing\n    82\t    \"any payload value is stored and retrieved unchanged; nil is a\n    83\t            legal opaque payload\"\n    84\t    (doseq [p [nil 42 \"hello\" :kw [1 2 3] {:a 1} #{:x :y} [:a [:b]]]]\n    85\t      (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)\n    86\t            address (jing/materialize! h p)]\n    87\t        (is (= (jing/segment-key p) address) (str \"address of \" (pr-str p)))\n    88\t        (is (= p (jing/get h address ::missing))\n    89\t            (str \"round trip of \" (pr-str p)))))))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(deftest insert-is-idempotent\n    93\t  (testing\n    94\t    \"the first put reports :inserted; an equal payload reports\n    95\t            :present and is never overwritten\"\n    96\t    (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)\n    97\t          payload {:x 42}\n    98\t          address (jing/segment-key payload)]\n    99\t      (is (= :inserted ((:put-content-fn h) address payload)))\n   100\t      (is (= :present ((:put-content-fn h) address payload)))\n   101\t      (is (= payload (jing/get h address ::missing)))\n   102\t      (is (= {address payload} (:content @(:state h))))))\n   103\t  (testing \"materialize! is idempotent end to end\"\n   104\t    (let [h (mem/create-content-mem)\n   105\t          payload {:x 42}]\n   106\t      (is (= (jing/materialize! h payload) (jing/materialize! h payload)))\n   107\t      (is (= 1 (count (:content @(:state h))))))))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(deftest put-rejects-invalid-content-addresses\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '482,666p' docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md | nl -ba -v482\"","aggregated_output":"   482\t## What is built, in four phases\n   483\t\n   484\tEach phase builds something checkable on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd, deletes\n   485\twhat it replaces, and leaves the suite green. Order is by dependency: the\n   486\tcore first, because three callers go through it and two of them ship today;\n   487\tthe file backend depends only on B and D; the pool depends on the core and on\n   488\tboth ends of the pool being v2; the prose depends on all three being real.\n   489\t\n   490\t### P0 — The core step, and its two shipped callers\n   491\t\n   492\t**Build** `src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc` per Decision 0: `step`,\n   493\trequiring only `dao.stream`. Refactor `dao.stream.forward/forward-step`\n   494\tinto its loop over `observe/step`, moving `malformed-result` into the core;\n   495\trefactor `yin.vm.stream-observer/observe-next` and `run-on-stream` over\n   496\tit; `attach`, every export and every result shape unchanged. This is one\n   497\tphase, not three, because the proof that the core is right *is* that both\n   498\tcallers' suites do not move: landing the core without refactoring them would\n   499\tprove nothing, and refactoring one without the other would leave the core\n   500\twith a single caller and no evidence it generalizes.\n   501\t\n   502\t**Delete** nothing outside the two refactored bodies.\n   503\t\n   504\t**Prove** with the new `test/dao/stream/observe_test.cljc`:\n   505\tdeclaration-driven classification — every outcome in\n   506\t`dao.stream/outcomes-next` maps to exactly one `:status`, every answer in\n   507\t`outcomes-append` from the effect likewise, an out-of-set or non-map read\n   508\tanswer is `:defect` with `:outcome :dao.stream/transport-error` and the raw\n   509\tanswer under `:read`, an out-of-set effect answer is `:failed` likewise under\n   510\t`:effect`; the effect is called exactly once, only on a read `ok`, with the\n   511\tobserved value; a throwing effect propagates with no result returned; the\n   512\tcursor is the successor on `:advance` and unchanged on every other status;\n   513\t`:recovery` is present exactly on `:gap`. And, unchanged: `forward_test`'s\n   514\tfive, `stream_observer_test`'s seventeen, `serving_test`, the ws and slice\n   515\tsuites, the REPL v2 suites, and `continuation_handoff_v2` — on each host, as\n   516\tthe evidence that nothing observable changed. Confirm `Testing\n   517\tdao.stream.observe-test` in the Node output.\n   518\t\n   519\t### P1 — The file backend\n   520\t\n   521\t**Build** `dao.jing.file` from F1–F6: `create-content-file` returning\n   522\t`{:put-content-fn :get-content-fn :close-fn}` over a private framed file —\n   523\topen or create, truncate an incomplete tail, replay, append-and-sync — with\n   524\t`records` for F5. Three host branches (`RandomAccessFile`, Node synchronous\n   525\t`fs`, `dart:io` `RandomAccessFile`), `#?(:cljd … :clj … :cljs …)` with `:cljd`\n   526\tfirst; `#?(:clj …)` alone does not exclude code from the cljd build.\n   527\t\n   528\t**Delete** `src/cljc/dao/stream/log.cljc` and `test/dao/stream/log_test.cljc`\n   529\t— its only consumer was this backend, and its `defopen :append-log` is a\n   530\tload-time registration into the ambient v1 registry. `dao.stream.file`\n   531\t(live-tail `:file`, consumed by `yin.io.file`) is a different transport and\n   532\tis untouched. Delete the old `file_test.cljc`.\n   533\t\n   534\t**Prove** with a new `file_test.cljc` written from F1–F6 and D1–D5: round trip\n   535\tof every payload kind including `nil`; `:inserted` then `:present` with an\n   536\tunchanged record count; durability across close and reopen; acknowledged\n   537\tinsert survives immediate close; equal duplicate records recover; collision\n   538\ton replay fails the open; each fail-closed category (malformed EDN, wrong\n   539\tshape, invalid address, hash mismatch) fails the open; truncation of an\n   540\toverlong-length tail, a sub-prefix tail, and a negative length, each followed\n   541\tby a clean put and reopen, with the torn bytes hand-written per host; put and\n   542\tget throw after close, close idempotent; JVM contention writes exactly one\n   543\trecord. `btree_durability_test`'s `file-close-reopen-recovery-test` runs\n   544\tunchanged as a consumer check (one stale comment fixed).\n   545\t\n   546\t### P2 — The pool, its two ends, and the in-memory backend\n   547\t\n   548\t**Build** in `dao.jing`: `observer-state`, `observe-step!`, `adopt-cursor`\n   549\tper Decision 1 over `dao.stream.observe/step`, requiring `dao.stream`\n   550\tand `dao.stream.observe`; the content-addressing core (A, B, C, D) is\n   551\talready what the invariants say and is kept. Keep `dao.jing.mem` (it\n   552\tsatisfies B and D), dropping the D4 pins. Move the pool's writer end to v2:\n   553\t`dao.space.index/append-ok!` (`index.cljc:526-531`) appends with\n   554\t`dao.stream/append!` and requires `:dao.stream/ok`; the transactor's\n   555\tintake validation (`transactor.cljc:197-201`) uses `dao.stream/writer?`.\n   556\tThe pool is one thing with two ends, and `dao.jing.md` §Publication names\n   557\t`publish-index!` as its writer; the rest of `dao.space` — the agent-local\n   558\tstream, `snapshot-datoms`, the transactor's own protocols, the published-index\n   559\t`defopen`, `dao.space.query` — is its own plan's.\n   560\t\n   561\t**Delete** the old observer functions and their `dao.stream` require from\n   562\t`dao.jing`; the observer section of `jing_test.cljc` and its v1 fixtures; the\n   563\tv1 `open-stream` helpers in `mem_test.cljc` and `dht_test.cljc`; the\n   564\t`open-intake` helpers in the five `test/dao/space/` files.\n   565\t\n   566\t**Prove** with `jing_test.cljc` rewritten from A–E over v2 ring buffers\n   567\t(`ringbuffer/create!`, cursors from `stream/cursor … :dao.stream/oldest`):\n   568\tknown-answer digests on every host; address determinism, order-insensitivity,\n   569\ttotality, cross-type distinctness, EDN readability, `segment-hash`\n   570\tstrictness; `materialize!` derivation, verdict vocabulary, `:present`\n   571\tread-back with the absent and unequal failures, idempotence, no stamp; `get`\n   572\tstrictness before the backend and not-found; handle-fn presence and `close!`\n   573\tdelegation; the pool — plain-data state, missing cursor and non-reader throw,\n   574\tempty pool blocked, all blocked, hashing and retrieval, convergence from two\n   575\tmembers, blocked and ended members do not prevent later ones, all ended,\n   576\tdrains then end, fairness (a continuously ready member yields), the\n   577\tpoison-payload case showing E5 through the seam, `gap` on a capacity-2\n   578\tbuffer with three appends (reported with `:member` and recovery cursor,\n   579\tcursor unchanged, other member progresses, reported again next turn,\n   580\t`adopt-cursor` then materializes the live value), the three defect outcomes\n   581\tand an out-of-set answer from a scripted reader, each carrying `:result`,\n   582\tdeclaration-driven totality over `outcomes-next`, members round-trip through\n   583\t`observer-state`. `mem_test.cljc` rewritten from B, D, D5 and one\n   584\tpool-convergence case; `dht_test.cljc:402`'s pool case and the five\n   585\t`dao.space` drains rewritten over v2 intakes with `:dao.stream/…` signals,\n   586\t`gap` fatal as before (E11). Confirm `Testing dao.jing-test` in the Node\n   587\toutput.\n   588\t\n   589\t### P3 — `dao.jing.md`\n   590\t\n   591\tWrite the [T→D] invariants into the design — A3, A4 into *Canonical\n   592\tencoding*; B5, B6 into *Materialization rule*; D3 into *Resource lifecycle*;\n   593\tF6 into the file backend's entry. Rewrite *The intake pool* and *Cursor\n   594\ttracking and recovery* to Decision 1's entry shape, cursor discipline and\n   595\tsignal table, and say that the observation step is `dao.stream.observe`,\n   596\tshared with `forward` and the VM, and that E5 is a property of that seam.\n   597\tRewrite *Implemented surface*: the file backend as \"a content-addressed store\n   598\tbacked by a private framed append-only file\" (Decision 2's design-document\n   599\tchange, routed as such); `dao.jing.remote` as awaiting `dao.space`'s plan\n   600\twith Decision 3 as its target. *Open items*: durable checkpoints store\n   601\twhatever cursor value the transport minted, serializability TBD in the\n   602\tcontract; add **\"the content write path as an effect stream\"** per\n   603\tDecision 2. Untouched: *Definition*, *Publication*, *Storage ignorance*,\n   604\t*Physical intake versus semantic composition*, *Reads*, *Lineage*,\n   605\t`dao.jing.dht.md`.\n   606\t\n   607\t## Host matrix\n   608\t\n   609\t| phase | clj | cljs (Node) | cljd | notes |\n   610\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   611\t| P0 | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | pure `.cljc`; `forward`, VM, serving, ws and REPL suites unchanged; cljd lane regenerates `test/cljd-out/` |\n   612\t| P1 | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | three host branches in `dao.jing.file`; torn-tail bytes hand-written per host |\n   613\t| P2 | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | pure `.cljc` |\n   614\t| P3 | — | — | — | prose |\n   615\t\n   616\t## Invariants of the whole, checked\n   617\t\n   618\tNo hidden global state: `dao.stream.observe` and `dao.jing` hold no atom;\n   619\tbackend state is per-handle; P1 removes a `defopen` from the ambient\n   620\tregistry. No implicit control flow: `step` and `observe-step!` return; the\n   621\tcomposition calls again. No callbacks in any surface touched: the effect is\n   622\tan argument the caller passes and the step calls once, synchronously, before\n   623\treturning — the same shape as `forward-step`'s policies, not a continuation\n   624\thanded to host machinery. No shared mutable state. Interpretation and\n   625\texecution separate: the step observes, the effect executes, the caller\n   626\tcoordinates. No assumed graphs.\n   627\t\n   628\t## Boundary\n   629\t\n   630\t**Built or deleted here:** `dao.stream.observe` (new), the loop bodies of\n   631\t`dao.stream.forward` and `yin.vm.stream-observer` (exports unchanged),\n   632\t`dao.jing`, `dao.jing.file`, `dao.jing.mem` (kept), `dao.stream.log`\n   633\t(deleted), the two writer seams in `dao.space.index` and\n   634\t`dao.space.transactor`, `observe_test` (new), `jing_test`, `mem_test`,\n   635\t`file_test`, `log_test` (deleted), the pool cases in `dht_test` and the five\n   636\t`dao.space` tests, one comment in `btree_durability_test`, `dao.jing.md`.\n   637\t\n   638\t**Not here, each with its home:** `dao.jing.remote`, `remote_test` and\n   639\t`dao.jing.coordinate`'s remote branch — Decision 3, `dao.space`'s plan;\n   640\t`dao.jing.dht*` — the UDP transport, deferred by the stream plan; everything\n   641\telse in `dao.space*` — its own plan; the content write path as an effect\n   642\tstream — a DaoJing architecture item; a content-serving endpoint — whatever\n   643\tproduct surface needs it; canonical encoding, durable checkpoints and a\n   644\trunner, materialization acknowledgement, garbage collection — `dao.jing.md`'s\n   645\topen items, unchanged.\n   646\t\n   647\t## End condition\n   648\t\n   649\tOn clj, cljs (Node) and cljd: `dao.stream.observe` exists, requires only\n   650\t`dao.stream`, and `dao.stream.forward`, `yin.vm.stream-observer` and\n   651\t`dao.jing` all observe through it, with `forward`'s five and the VM's\n   652\tseventeen tests unchanged and green; `dao.jing`, `dao.jing.file` and\n   653\t`dao.jing.mem` require no `dao.stream*` namespace; every invariant A–F has a\n   654\ttest that exercises it, the E group on the side of the seam that guarantees\n   655\tit, and the [T→D] ones are in `dao.jing.md`; `dao.stream.log` is gone;\n   656\t`dao.space`'s pool writers accept v2 writers and every `dao.space` suite is\n   657\tgreen over v2 intakes; `dao.jing.remote`, `dao.jing.coordinate`'s remote\n   658\tbranch and `dao.jing.dht*` are the only things under `dao.jing*` still on v1,\n   659\tand this document says why.\n   660\t\n   661\t---\n   662\t\n   663\t## What changed from revision 8, and why\n   664\t\n   665\t- **Decision 0 corrected, and the proposal accepted.** Revision 8 used\n   666\t  `forward` as a location precedent and copied the step's design from the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '196,420p' docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md | nl -ba -v196\"","aggregated_output":"   196\t## Decisions\n   197\t\n   198\t### Decision 0 — One core step, with `forward` as its first caller\n   199\t\n   200\t**The correction to revision 8.** Revision 8 cited `dao.stream.forward` as\n   201\t\"the precedent for a transport-agnostic interpreter step living under the\n   202\tcontract's namespace\" — a claim about where a file may live — and never asked\n   203\twhether `forward` made the new file unnecessary. It also took the step's\n   204\tdesign from `yin.vm.stream-observer`, the caller that hardcoded its\n   205\tpolicies, when the stronger design was in `forward`: outcomes as data under\n   206\t`:status` (`forward.cljc:135-138,163-166`), gap policy as a caller-supplied\n   207\tparameter (`61-67,86-92`), and the cursor advanced only after the effect\n   208\tsucceeds (`130`). `forward` got it right; revision 8 proposed writing it\n   209\tagain beside it. That was wrong.\n   210\t\n   211\t**The test applied, and where it lands.** A core is real only if it stays\n   212\tparameter-light: if serving three callers needs `:gap-policy` *and*\n   213\t`:batch-budget` *and* a terminal-naming function, three clear implementations\n   214\twere right. Walked honestly against all three callers, the core needs\n   215\t**three parameters and no policy**: a source, a cursor, and an effect. The\n   216\tgap policy is a decision the caller makes on the returned `:gap`; the budget\n   217\tis a loop the caller writes around the step; terminal naming\n   218\t(`:source-ended`, `:destination-closed`) is a rename the caller applies to\n   219\t`:status` and `:outcome`. Every one of `forward`'s subtleties — the resume\n   220\tallowance, the fixed-point rule, terminal-state re-stepping as a no-op — is\n   221\tloop-level and stays in `forward`. The factoring passes. It is not\n   222\tover-abstraction; it is the shape all three already have, written once:\n   223\t\n   224\t```\n   225\tread one value at cursor\n   226\t  ok       → run the effect on the value\n   227\t               ok           → advance to the successor\n   228\t               not yet      → keep the cursor, retry later\n   229\t               failed       → stop\n   230\t  blocked  → keep the cursor\n   231\t  end      → keep the cursor\n   232\t  gap      → hand back the recovery cursor; the caller decides\n   233\t  defect   → stop, raw answer retained\n   234\t```\n   235\t\n   236\t**The core: `dao.stream.observe/step`.** A new namespace requiring only\n   237\t`dao.stream`. Stateless, no loop, one function:\n   238\t\n   239\t```clojure\n   240\t(observe/step source cursor effect)\n   241\t;; effect: (fn [value] -> outcome-map) answering with the writer outcome set —\n   242\t;;   :dao.stream/ok, /full (\"not yet\"), /invalid-value, /closed, /transport-error.\n   243\t;;   Any other answer is classified as /transport-error with the raw answer\n   244\t;;   retained (forward's malformed-result rule). A throwing effect propagates\n   245\t;;   before any advance exists.\n   246\t;;\n   247\t;; returns, always with :cursor and :read (the raw next result):\n   248\t;;   {:status :advance :cursor successor :effect e}                 ; effect ok\n   249\t;;   {:status :retry   :cursor cursor :outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n   250\t;;   {:status :retry   :cursor cursor :outcome :dao.stream/full :effect e}\n   251\t;;   {:status :ended   :cursor cursor :outcome :dao.stream/end}\n   252\t;;   {:status :gap     :cursor cursor :outcome :dao.stream/gap :recovery c'}\n   253\t;;   {:status :defect  :cursor cursor :outcome k}                   ; source: cursor-mismatch, invalid-cursor, transport-error, or a malformed read\n   254\t;;   {:status :failed  :cursor cursor :outcome k :effect e}         ; effect: invalid-value, closed, transport-error, or a malformed effect answer\n   255\t```\n   256\t\n   257\t`:retry` from the effect is produced only by an effect with a \"not yet\"\n   258\tanswer — today only `forward`'s `append!` answering `full`. A function\n   259\teffect that wraps `materialize!` or `load-program` answers `ok` or throws, so\n   260\tthe branch costs it nothing. The effect-answer convention — the writer\n   261\toutcome set — is the one real coupling the core imposes; both function\n   262\tcallers meet it with a two-line wrapper, and it is what lets `forward` pass\n   263\t`append!` through unwrapped.\n   264\t\n   265\t**`forward` refactors onto it with no behavioural change.** `forward-step`\n   266\tkeeps its namespace, signature, options, `initial-state` and\n   267\t`default-options`, and becomes the loop it already is over `observe/step`\n   268\twith `(fn [v] (stream/append! destination v))` as the effect: `:advance` →\n   269\t`recur next-cursor (dec remaining) resumes (inc forwarded)`; `:retry` →\n   270\t`result-state cursor :retry forwarded outcome` for both `blocked` and `full`,\n   271\texactly as `blocked-and-full-do-not-advance-cursor` pins; `:gap` → the\n   272\texisting `cond` — policy via `gap-action`, fixed point when\n   273\t`(= recovery cursor)` terminates as `:source-gap`, resume while the\n   274\tallowance lasts, else `:continue` at the recovery cursor; `:ended` and\n   275\t`:defect` → `terminal-status :source`; `:failed` → `terminal-status\n   276\t:destination`. The terminal-state no-op on re-step (`108-111`) and the\n   277\tbudget-zero early return stay in front of the loop. The `malformed-result`\n   278\tguard moves into the core, where both `next` and the effect answer are\n   279\tclassified, and `forward` keeps its `:transport-error` `:outcome` on the same\n   280\tinputs. Its five tests — `forwards-a-bounded-batch`,\n   281\t`blocked-and-full-do-not-advance-cursor`, `gap-policy-is-explicit`,\n   282\t`gap-resume-is-bounded-and-total`,\n   283\t`terminal-outcomes-are-explicit-and-no-close-is-implied` — change no\n   284\tassertion. Its one production consumer, `dao.stream.serving`, calls\n   285\t`forward-step`, `initial-state` and `default-options` (`serving.cljc:131,255,312`)\n   286\tand is untouched.\n   287\t\n   288\t**The VM refactors onto it with no behavioural change.**\n   289\t`yin.vm.stream-observer` keeps `attach`, `observe-next` and\n   290\t`run-on-stream` with their shapes. `observe-next` is `observe/step` with a\n   291\tnull effect (`(fn [_] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})`): `:advance` →\n   292\t`{:status :ok :batch (get-in r [:read :dao.stream/value]) :observer observer'}`;\n   293\t`:retry` (blocked) and `:ended` retain the cursor; `:gap` adopts `:recovery`\n   294\tand increments `:ingress-gaps`; `:defect` throws with the *original* read\n   295\toutcome from `:read` — so `observe-next-throws-on-terminal-and-unexpected-outcomes-test`\n   296\tstill sees the unexpected keyword it scripted, not the core's classification\n   297\t— plus `:cursor` and `:ingress-gaps` as today. `run-on-stream` uses\n   298\t`observe/step` with `(fn [batch] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :vm\n   299\t(load-program vm batch)})` as the effect, runs `run-vm` on the loaded VM, and\n   300\tpublishes the session after both; a throwing loader propagates inside the\n   301\tcore before any advance, which is `a-failing-loader-leaves-the-old-cursor-for-a-retry-test`\n   302\tunchanged. The gap auto-advance and the terminal throw are now visibly the\n   303\tVM's policy, applied to the core's data. None of its 17 tests changes an\n   304\tassertion; `yin.repl.core` and `continuation_handoff_v2` consume the VM\n   305\tnamespace only.\n   306\t\n   307\t**What is not shared**, as in revision 8: attachment (the anchor is the\n   308\tcomposition's policy; the VM keeps `attach`, DaoJing has none); state (the\n   309\tcore has none, so `:ingress-gaps` never enters the seam); coordination\n   310\t(`forward`'s budget loop, the VM's `run-on-stream`, DaoJing's round-robin\n   311\tpool — three different loops over one step).\n   312\t\n   313\t**Layering.** `dao.stream.observe` sits where `forward` sits: an\n   314\tinterpreter over the contract, owned by neither storage nor the VM, requiring\n   315\tonly `dao.stream`. `forward` keeps its namespace as the thin layer that\n   316\tadds the loop, the resume allowance and the naming, because that is what it\n   317\tis now and what its consumer imports.\n   318\t\n   319\t### Decision 1 — DaoJing's observer, built on the step\n   320\t\n   321\tDaoJing's observer is pool coordination over `observe/step` with\n   322\t`materialize!` as the effect. Entry shape `{:stream <v2 reader handle>\n   323\t:cursor <opaque> :status s}`; `observer-state` validates E3 and holds\n   324\t`{:members [...] :next i}`; `adopt-cursor` is the one other cursor mutation.\n   325\tOne call of `observe-step!` walks the pool once from `:next`:\n   326\t\n   327\t```clojure\n   328\t;; per member, in turn:\n   329\t(observe/step stream cursor\n   330\t              (fn [payload] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   331\t                             :address (jing/materialize! handle payload)}))\n   332\t;; :advance → member cursor := successor, status :dao.stream/ok, :next := after this member;\n   333\t;;            return {:signal :dao.stream/ok :address (get-in r [:effect :address])}\n   334\t;; :retry   → status :dao.stream/blocked, continue the walk\n   335\t;; :ended   → status :dao.stream/end, continue the walk\n   336\t;; :gap     → status recorded, :next := after this member;\n   337\t;;            return {:signal :dao.stream/gap :member i :cursor (:recovery r)}\n   338\t;; :defect  → status recorded, :next := after this member;\n   339\t;;            return {:signal (:outcome r) :member i :result (:read r)}\n   340\t;; :failed  → impossible: the effect answers ok or throws (E5)\n   341\t;; walk exhausted → {:signal :dao.stream/end} if every member ended, else {:signal :dao.stream/blocked}\n   342\t```\n   343\t\n   344\tSignal table:\n   345\t\n   346\t| signal | when | extra keys | member cursor |\n   347\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   348\t| `:dao.stream/ok` | a payload was materialized | `:address` | successor, from the step |\n   349\t| `:dao.stream/blocked` | empty pool, or every non-ended member blocked | — | unchanged |\n   350\t| `:dao.stream/end` | every member has ended | — | unchanged |\n   351\t| `:dao.stream/gap` | member `i`'s position was evicted | `:member i`, `:cursor` (the step's `:recovery`) | unchanged |\n   352\t| `/cursor-mismatch`, `/invalid-cursor`, `/transport-error` | member `i`'s read failed, or answered outside the contract | `:member i`, `:result` (the step's `:read`) | unchanged |\n   353\t\n   354\tWhat the pool adds to the step is exactly E1, E3, E6, E8 and the reporting\n   355\thalf of E9; what it inherits is E2's successor discipline, E4's totality, E5\n   356\tstructurally, E9's raw read and recovery cursor as data, and E10.\n   357\t\n   358\t### Decision 2 — The durable log is not a stream\n   359\t\n   360\t`dao.jing.file` writes its own framed file. It does not use a stream\n   361\ttransport, and none is built for it.\n   362\t\n   363\t**Why.** The file has one reader — the backend itself, once, at open — and\n   364\tone writer — the backend's own put. No cursor is ever handed out, no\n   365\tdescriptor projected, nothing attaches, and the file never sits in a pool.\n   366\tEvery property the contract exists to guarantee is unused, and a transport\n   367\twith one consumer would owe the conformance suite for nobody. The parallel is\n   368\t`dao.jing.mem`: a private atom behind the backend effects; `dao.jing.md`\n   369\talready says \"backend effects are explicit functions, not a protocol or\n   370\thidden state.\" Wrapping the file as a public `:dao.stream/type` also made\n   371\tDaoJing's storage format a transport anyone could open.\n   372\t\n   373\t**Why a v2 append-log is not an alternative.** It is constructible —\n   374\t`append!`'s `ok` \"implies neither local readability nor remote delivery\"\n   375\t(`dao.stream.md`, Writing) — but it cannot supply what F1 needs: `:inserted`\n   376\tmeans \"durably stored now\", and an `ok` that disclaims durability cannot\n   377\thonestly become it. Either the transport grows a transport-owned durability\n   378\tsignal contract-generic code may not reach for, or `materialize!`'s contract\n   379\tchanges so durability arrives later as data, which reaches\n   380\t`dao.data.btree.storage` and `dao.space.index`. That is the write-path\n   381\tredesign, not a transport choice.\n   382\t\n   383\t**The pre-existing question.** `datom.world.md:66-68`: an adapter that exposes\n   384\ta function for portable code to call \"keeps the coupling, and the effect\n   385\tnever appears as an emission.\" `:put-content-fn` is such a function, whatever\n   386\tsits beneath it. Whether DaoJing's synchronous content handle conforms to Host\n   387\tBoundaries is real, is not created here, and is cured by no transport. P3\n   388\trecords it in `dao.jing.md`'s open items as **\"the content write path as an\n   389\teffect stream\"** — durability as data, `materialize!` no longer returning an\n   390\taddress synchronously — out of scope here because of its reach. The design\n   391\there is compatible with that future: `datom.world.md:57-59` puts raw host\n   392\toperations inside the host interpreter, which is where this leaves the file\n   393\tIO.\n   394\t\n   395\t**Recorded dissent.** `gpt-5.6-sol` holds that direct file IO behind\n   396\t`:put-content-fn` violates `datom.world.md:53-68` and a v2 append-log should\n   397\tbe built. The plan holds the violation, if any, is the synchronous handle\n   398\titself. `glm-5.3` and `gpt-6-astra` accept the plan's position.\n   399\t\n   400\t### Decision 3 — The remote store: deferred, design recorded\n   401\t\n   402\t**Why it is deferred, and why that is not legacy.** `jing/get` answers\n   403\tsynchronously; `dao.stream.rpc` cannot answer synchronously on any host —\n   404\tby contract, no operation waits, and on cljs and cljd there is nothing to wait\n   405\twith. So a remote content store cannot present a local store's interface,\n   406\tand that is true of code written from scratch today with no v1 anywhere. What\n   407\ta remote store *is* — a client the caller steps, whose answers arrive as\n   408\tcompletions — changes what `dao.space.index` does to restore a B-tree from a\n   409\tremote coordinate, which is the async hydration `dao.data.btree.md` §5.4\n   410\tdefers, and belongs to `dao.space`'s plan. It is the one thing here that a\n   411\tfree rewrite does not dissolve. The current `dao.jing.remote`, its tests, and\n   412\t`dao.jing.coordinate`'s JVM `:dao.jing/remote` branch stay as they are until\n   413\tthat plan; nothing else in `dao.jing*` depends on them.\n   414\t\n   415\t**The design, for that plan.** Server side: `default-handlers` — `:jing/put-content`\n   416\treturns `:inserted`/`:present`, `:jing/get-content` returns the exact envelope\n   417\t`{:found? boolean :value v}` — served by `dao.stream.apply/serve-once!`;\n   418\tB6 holds at the server's door. Client side:\n   419\t\n   420\t```clojure\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
